## Workspace Topology

This is a **pnpm workspace monorepo** orchestrator. All deliverable code lives in
`packages/*`. The workspace root does not deploy itself — child packages handle
their own deployment pipelines.

```
<%workload%>/
├── packages/
│   ├── example/          # starter package (replace or delete)
│   └── <your-package>/   # add more here
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml   # declares packages/* as workspace members
├── package.json          # root: workspace-wide scripts (build, test, lint, typecheck)
├── tsconfig.base.json    # base TS config — each package extends this
├── biome.jsonc           # linting/formatting (runs at root, covers all packages)
├── AGENTS.md             # this file
└── README.md
```

## Tech Stack

| Aspect | Choice |
|---|---|
| Package manager | pnpm workspace |
| Runtime | Node <%node_version%> |
| Language | TypeScript (strict) |
| Lint + format | Biome v2 (root-level, applies to all packages) |
| Tests | Vitest (per package) |
| Archetype | monorepo-root |

## Commands

```bash
pnpm install              # install all workspace packages
pnpm dev                  # run dev in all packages (parallel)
pnpm build                # build all packages
pnpm test                 # test all packages
pnpm lint                 # biome check across the entire workspace
pnpm typecheck            # tsc --noEmit in every package
```

To operate on a single package:

```bash
pnpm --filter @<%workload%>/example test
pnpm --filter @<%workload%>/example typecheck
```

## Branching

- `staging` — working branch
- `main` — production (CI release-please publishes from here, if enabled)

## Critical Context

- **No source at root**: The workspace root contains only orchestration config.
  Do not add `src/` or `tests/` to the root — put code in `packages/*`.
- **Each package owns its deploy**: If a package needs Azure deployment, apply
  the appropriate janus archetype overlay inside that package directory and add
  its CI/CD workflow to `.github/workflows/`.
- **Biome runs at root**: The root `biome.jsonc` covers all files in the workspace.
  Run `pnpm lint` from root, not from inside packages.
- **tsconfig.base.json**: Each package's `tsconfig.json` should `"extends":
  "../../tsconfig.base.json"` (adjust the relative path for deeper nesting).
- **Adding a package**: Create `packages/<name>/package.json` with
  `"name": "@<%workload%>/<name>"`, add appropriate `scripts.build`, `scripts.test`,
  and `scripts.typecheck`, then run `pnpm install` at root to link it.
- **Turborepo**: Not included by default. Add only if the number of packages
  grows beyond ~10 or build caching becomes worthwhile.

